#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-lang-plan R1: the Scheme reader validates a dotted pair's shape --
;; exactly one datum may follow the `.` -- rather than reading the `.` as an
;; ordinary symbol and leaving elaboration to notice.  The other two shapes
;; (`(. b)`, `(a .)`) get their own messages; this pins the common typo.
(defn main [] : int
  (println (quote (a . b c)))
  0)
